      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T12:11:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion. I wasn\u0027t able to trigger an actual NVLink port\nhealth event on the device to validate the decode end to end — using Set\nPort Health Thresholds (0x07) to lower a threshold and get a real event to\nfire wasn\u0027t something I could reliably reproduce on the available hardware.\n\nFor now the decode is covered by unit-test vectors that match the documented\non-wire event payload (portNumber + reserved + 32-bit threshold bitmap).\n\nI\u0027d like to track the on-device, 0x07-triggered validation as a follow-up\nsurvey item rather than block this change on it.",
